# oracle: pair_style smtbq with the Al2O3 potential (ffield.smtbq.Al2O3, QEqAll) on a 109-atom sphere (R 12 A about the centre, 68 O and 41 Al) cut from examples/PACKAGES/smtbq/data.Alpha (the 1800-atom alumina of in.smtbq.Al2O3), free boundaries (boundary f f f, the cluster is not periodic), 10 NVE steps from 300 K with the example's charge computes. The charges are equilibrated inside the pair style every step (Nevery 1)
# native: LAMMPS b332f28 built from source with -D PKG_SMTBQ=on -D PKG_MANYBODY=on -D PKG_KSPACE=on -D PKG_MOLECULE=on -D PKG_EXTRA-FIX=on (the scratch build of the SMTBQ package, the installed lmp has no SMTBQ)
# oracle-inputs: w189sq_al2o3_cluster.data
# oracle-potentials: ffield.smtbq.Al2O3
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# Measured with native LAMMPS: thermo max relative error 7.0e-12, per-atom 2.0e-11 (QEq every step; engine ~2.2 s).
units           metal
atom_style      charge
dimension       3
boundary        f f f
read_data       w189sq_al2o3_cluster.data
mass            1 16.00
mass            2 26.98
group           Oxy type 1
compute         chargeOxy Oxy property/atom q
compute         q_Oxy Oxy reduce ave c_chargeOxy
group           Al type 2
compute         chargeAl Al property/atom q
compute         q_Al Al reduce ave c_chargeAl
velocity        all create 300 277387
pair_style      smtbq
pair_coeff      * * ffield.smtbq.Al2O3 O Al
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 20 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.0002
thermo_style    custom step temp press pe ke etotal c_q_Al c_q_Oxy lx ly lz vol
thermo_modify   format float %.15g flush yes
thermo          1
fix             3 all nve
run             10
